+ * By default, on success (ESP_OK) the callback must ensure the completion signal is triggered
+ * (e.g. by calling @c esp_lcd_panel_draw_bitmap internally so its done-ISR fires). A callback
+ * which splits one logical LVGL flush into multiple synchronous panel transfers must set
+ * @c waits_until_complete. The adapter then ignores intermediate color-transfer completion
+ * events and completes the logical LVGL flush once, after the callback returns.
+ *
+ * On failure the adapter calls @c lv_display_flush_ready / task-notify itself as a fallback,
+ * so the flush handshake always completes.
